  "id": "COMPOUND:26205 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "Eburnamenine appears to interact with Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform through a series of molecular targets, with the replicase polyprotein 1a acting as a central mediator. This polyprotein is targeted by multiple compounds, including 3Beta,6Alpha-Dihydroxylup-20(29)-Ene and 2-(2,5-Dihydroxyphenyl)-3,5-dihydroxy-6,7,8-trimethoxychromen-4-one, all of which are implicated in targeting the phosphatase subunit. The evidence suggests that Eburnamenine may exert its effects by modulating the activity of this phosphatase, potentially through the replication of viral proteins that are substrates of the phosphatase. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with the phosphatase subunit indicates a possible mechanism involving the regulation of viral replication and the subsequent modulation of cellular signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the phosphatase in the biological response to Eburnamenine, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
